      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>LXIIII. Gif feorcund<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-5"/> mon oððe fremde butan wege geond wudu gonge ⁊ ne hrieme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-4"/> ne horn blawe, for ðeof he bið to profianne: oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.3-4"/> to sleanne oððe to áliesanne.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>LXIIII. Gif forcund<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-3"/> mon oððe fremde buton wege geond wudu gonge ⁊ ne hrime ne horn blawe, for ðeof he bið to profianne: oððe to sleanne oððe to lesanne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="98" ed="#liebermann"/>LXIIII. Gif feorcund<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-4"/> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-3"/> oððe fremde buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-3"/> wege geond wudu gonge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-3"/> ⁊ ne hryme ne horn blawe, for ðeof he bið to profianne: oððe to sleanne oþþe to lysanne.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.3-3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Be feorran cumenan m<hi rend="italic">en</hi>. Gyf feorcuman man oððe fre<hi rend="italic">m</hi>de butan wege geon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.1"/> wudu gonge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.2"/> ⁊ ne ryme ne horn blawe, for ðeof he bið to profianne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.3"/> oððe to alysenne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis alienigena uel ignotus sine uia uadat in nemus, ut nec ore clamet nec cornu sonet, pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-2"/> fure probandus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-2"/> est: uel occidendus uel etiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_20.lnote.oe.3-2"/> redimendus.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="42" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be feorran cumenan men.] Gif feorcund<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_20.attnote.fn.5"/> mon oððe fremde butan wege geond<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_20.attnote.fn.6"/> wudu gonge ⁊ ne hrieme ne horn blawe, for ðeof he bið to profianne, oððe to sleanne<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_20.attnote.fn.7"/> oððe to áliesanne<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Ine_20.attnote.fn.8"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="20" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="384" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXIIII} Gif feorcund mon oððe fremde butan wege geond wudu gonge ⁊ ne hrieme ne horn blawe, for ðeof he bið to profianne: oððe to sleanne oððe to áliesanne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="99" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_20.lnote.de.1"/> ein fernher stammender<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.lnote.de.2"/> Mann oder ein Fremder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_20.lnote.de.3"/> abseits<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_20.lnote.de.4"/> vom Wege durch den Wald<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_20.lnote.de.5"/> geht und weder ruft noch Horn bläst, als Dieb ist der zu erachten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_20.lnote.de.6"/>: entweder zu tödten oder auszulösen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_20.lnote.de.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a man of distant origin or a stranger goes through the wood off the road and neither shouts nor blows a horn, he is to be considered a thief: either to be killed or to be redeemed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="43" ed="#attenborough"/>If a man from afar, or a stranger, travels through a wood off the highway and neither shouts nor blows a horn, he shall be assumed to be a thief, and as such may be either slain or put to ransom.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_20.whinote.n.2"/><pb n="402" ed="#whitelock"/>If a man from a distance or a foreigner goes through the wood off the track, and does not shout nor blow a horn, he is to be assumed to be a thief, to be either killed or redeemed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="385" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If [either] a person who has come from far off or a stranger travels off the road through the woods and does not shout out or blow a horn, he is to be taken for a thief: either to be slain or to be redeemed [by ransom].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="402"><label>almost identical</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_28">Wi 28</ref> <quote>Almost identical with Wihtred 28.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="385"><label>paralleled</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_28">Wi 28</ref> <quote>This clause is paralleled in Wihtred §23 [L28].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="385"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-47">Af El 47</ref> <quote>MP §47 suggests that the problem was the stealthy approach and not simply mistrust of outsiders</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="385"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_28">Ine 28</ref> <quote>Compare §28, which allows a 10-shilling reward to one who captures a thief.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="50"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_28">Ine 28</ref> <quote>Ine §20/Wihtred §23 [L28] also seems to contradict Ine §28 – as it does Wihtred §21 [L26]</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="102"><ref target="clause:Wi_25">Wi 25–28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="103"><ref target="clause:Wi_28">Wi 28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="399"><ref target="clause:Wi_28">Wi 28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="44"><ref target="clause:Wi_28">Wi 28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="261"><ref target="clause:Af_El-to-47">Af El 47</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="395"><ref target="clause:Ine_28">Ine 28</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät geändert aus</hi> gonde</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered late from gonde</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ines lage <hi rend="italic">roth über der Seite</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ines lage in red at the head of the page</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. f. <hi rend="italic">doppelt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. f. twice in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">prob. — pro fure <hi rend="italic">in Cap.</hi> 21 <hi rend="italic">überspringt M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">prob. — pro fure in cap. 21 skipped by M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">99</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">perdendus</hi> <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">perdendus</hi> added by Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur; geänd. in</hi> alys.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure; altered to alys.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.1-5" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">feor cuman man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">feor cuman man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.2-4" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hryme <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hryme Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.3-4" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o. to sl. <hi rend="italic">überspringt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o. to sl. skipped by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">98</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">alys. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">alys. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diesen Satz benutzte Wi 28; <hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi>¹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Wi 28 made use of this sentence; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> there¹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B nimmt die Form der Rubrik (und Wi’s) auf</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B adopts the form of the rubric (and of Wi)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ähnlich braucht Agsä. Recht <hi rend="italic">uncuð,</hi> und daher wohl setzt Q <hi rend="italic">ignotus</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">A.-S. law uses <hi rend="italic">uncuð</hi> similarly, and that is probably why Q puts <hi rend="italic">ignotus</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Strasse 2. Ine trifft Vagabunden (Maurer <hi rend="italic">Kr. Übsch.</hi> I 65), schreckt nicht etwa Fremde (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4a) ab</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Strasse 2. Ine is aimed at vagabonds (Maurer <hi rend="italic">Kr. Übsch.</hi> I 65), not, say, at deterring strangers (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4a)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Grenzwald’ mit Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 46 im besonderen zu verstehen, liegt kein Grund vor. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Horn 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">There is no reason to understand it specifically as ‘boundary forest’, with Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 46. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Horn 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘beweisen’ oder ‘prüfen, verhören’. Auch ahd. <hi rend="italic">pruoven</hi> ‘wahrnehmen, schätzen’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘prove’ or ‘examine, interrogate’. OHG <hi rend="italic">pruoven</hi> also means ‘perceive, assess’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_20.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wer ihn gebunden vor Gericht bringt und den Tatbestand beschwört, erhält den Anzeigelohn; der Vagabund oder das Lösegeld für ihn gehört dem König. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> handhaft 11; Diebstahl 11b. c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Whoever brings him bound before the court and swears to the facts receives the informer’s reward; the vagabond, or the ransom for him, belongs to the king. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> handhaft 11; Diebstahl 11b. c</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_20.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>feorcund</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">feorcuman man</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_20.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>geond</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">geon</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_20.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>sleanne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">oððe to sleanne</hi>. om. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_20.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><label>áliesanne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">lesanne</hi>. Bu. <hi rend="italic">lysanne</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_20.attnote.n.0" n="0" source="#attenborough" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">185</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For the significance of this cap. see the introduction to the Laws of Ine and Alfred, p. 34.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_20.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">402</biblScope></bibl><label>20</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Almost identical with Wihtred 28.</seg></note>
      </div>
